  "description": "Cohere is a Canadian enterprise AI company headquartered in Toronto that builds foundation models and security-first, end-to-end AI products for private, VPC, on-premises, and sovereign deployment. Founded in 2019 by Aidan Gomez, Ivan Zhang, and Nick Frosst, it ships the Command, Embed, Rerank, Transcribe, Parse, and North Small Translate models alongside North, its enterprise AI workspace, and Model Vault for dedicated inference. Cohere raised $500 million at a $6.8 billion valuation in August 2025, and in 2026 agreed to combine with Germany's Aleph Alpha to form a transatlantic sovereign AI provider.",
